From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Umair Ahmed Shah <umairahmedshah@hotmail.com>
Date: Tue, 16 Jun 2026 11:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] plat-rz/g2l: relax int-conversion errors for gcc 14+

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [bringup workaround pending vendor source cleanup]

gcc 14 promoted -Wint-conversion and -Wincompatible-pointer-types from
warnings to default-errors. Multiple sites in plat-rz/common (r_sce
public/private, pta_sce, sflash callers) pass typed pointers where the
prototype declares uintptr_t, or vice versa. The OP-TEE 4.8 Renesas fork
predates this gcc change and has not been swept clean.

Demote these to warnings at the platform level so the build succeeds.
Diagnostics remain visible; remove this line once plat-rz source is
updated to compile clean against gcc 14+.

Signed-off-by: Umair Ahmed Shah <umairahmedshah@hotmail.com>
---
 core/arch/arm/plat-rz/g2l/rzg2l_conf.mk | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/core/arch/arm/plat-rz/g2l/rzg2l_conf.mk b/core/arch/arm/plat-rz/g2l/rzg2l_conf.mk
--- a/core/arch/arm/plat-rz/g2l/rzg2l_conf.mk
+++ b/core/arch/arm/plat-rz/g2l/rzg2l_conf.mk
@@ -44,3 +44,7 @@ ifeq ($(PLATFORM_FLAVOR),g2ul_smarc)
 else
 CFG_SPI_FLASH_DEV ?= MT25QU512ABB
 endif
+
+# gcc 14+ default-errors; vendor source predates the change.
+core-platform-cflags += -Wno-error=int-conversion
+core-platform-cflags += -Wno-error=incompatible-pointer-types
